---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'

const pageDescription = 'Voting Handbook'
---

<BaseLayout lang="en" pageDescription={pageDescription}>
  <article class="relative flex flex-col items-center justify-center">
    <h1
      class="title bg-gradient-to-r from-accent-two/85 via-accent-one/85 to-accent-two/85 bg-clip-text text-transparent dark:from-accent-two dark:via-accent-one dark:to-accent-two"
    >
      Voting Abroad
    </h1>

    <section class="mt-6 w-full">
      <h2 class="title mb-4 text-xl text-accent-two">
        Why It Is Important to Register to Vote and Participate in Elections
      </h2>
      <p>
        Serbia is, according to its constitution, a democratic republic, and
        elections represent the fundamental way for citizens to influence the
        governance of the country. However, in recent times, there have been
        various challenges related to the electoral process, which makes it
        important for all citizens to be active participants.
      </p>
      <p>
        Despite these challenges, parliamentary elections remain a key
        instrument for expressing the will of the citizens and for the changes
        we wish to see in society. Active participation can contribute to the
        fulfillment of various demands and goals.
      </p>
      <p>
        One of the challenges is the transparency of voter registry management,
        which makes it necessary for citizens, especially those in the diaspora,
        to be registered and informed to ensure the integrity of the electoral
        process.
      </p>
      <p>
        Registering to vote allows voters to become active and registered
        participants in elections. In this way, the diaspora not only exercises
        their rights but also contributes to protecting their identity and the
        integrity of the election process.
      </p>
      <p>
        Voting rights are not only exercised by voting itself but also through a
        responsible and engaged approach to elections. An active diaspora can be
        an important factor in the democratic development of our country.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-6 w-full">
      <h2 class="title mb-4 text-xl text-accent-two">
        Before the elections are announced
      </h2>

      <h3 class="text-l text-accent-three title mb-2">Voting eligibility</h3>
      <p>
        Citizens of Serbia with valid ID or passport are eligible to vote. If
        your passport has expired, you must apply for a new one at the nearest
        consulate.
      </p>
      <p>
        More info: <a
          class="text-accent-two underline-offset-2 hover:underline"
          href="https://www.mfa.gov.rs/gradjani/usluge/putne-isprave"
          target="_blank">mfa.gov.rs</a
        >
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-l text-accent-three title mb-2">
        Check the electoral roll
      </h3>
      <p>
        You must be registered to vote. Check your status at: <a
          class="text-accent-two underline-offset-2 hover:underline"
          href="https://upit.birackispisak.gov.rs"
          target="_blank">upit.birackispisak.gov.rs</a
        >
      </p>
      <p>If not listed, you can register only after elections are announced.</p>

      <h3 class="text-l text-accent-three title mb-2">
        Check Serbian Diplomatic Missions Worldwide
      </h3>
      <p>
        You can check them at: <a
          class="text-accent-two underline-offset-2 hover:underline"
          href="https://www.mfa.gov.rs/lat/predstavnistva/predstavnistva-srbije-u-svetu/ambasade"
          target="_blank">Serbian Diplomatic Missions</a
        >
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-6 w-full">
      <h2 class="title mb-4 text-xl text-accent-two">
        After elections are announced
      </h2>

      <h3 class="text-l text-accent-three title mb-2">
        Registering in the electoral roll
      </h3>
      <p>
        If you're not already registered, you must submit a request at least
        five days before the roll is finalized.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-l text-accent-three title mb-2">Voting from abroad</h3>
      <p>
        You must submit a request to vote from abroad regardless of previous
        participation. See the Law on the Unified Electoral Roll for details.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-l text-accent-three title mb-2">
        Request for voter information
      </h3>
      <p>
        It’s highly recommended to email the consulate requesting confirmation
        of your registration, even though it's not legally required.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-l text-accent-three title mb-2">Follow up on requests</h3>
      <p>
        Make sure your request was received by contacting the consulate (email,
        phone, or in person).
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-l text-accent-three title mb-2">
        Polling station determination
      </h3>
      <p>
        Polling stations are formed for 100–2,500 voters (with exceptions
        allowed by the RIK).
      </p>
      <p>
        Forms: <a
          class="text-accent-two underline-offset-2 hover:underline"
          href="https://www.eupropisi.com/dokumenti/SG_091_2023_002.docx"
          target="_blank">Official template</a
        >
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-6 w-full">
      <h2 class="title mb-4 text-xl text-accent-two">On election day</h2>

      <h3 class="text-l text-accent-three title mb-2">
        How to report irregularities
      </h3>
      <ul class="list-content list-inside list-disc" role="list">
        <li>Campaign materials near polling station</li>
        <li>Voting without proper ID</li>
        <li>Pressure by polling board members</li>
        <li>Unmarked voter lists or tampering</li>
        <li>Police presence without cause</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Request all irregularities to be noted in the official record.</p>
      <p>
        You can report within 24 hours. More info: <a
          class="text-accent-two underline-offset-2 hover:underline"
          href="https://www.cesid.rs/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/Vodi%C4%8D-za-za%C5%A1titu-izbornog-prava.pdf"
          target="_blank">CeSID Guide</a
        >
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
